WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.082 --> 00:00:06.850
PALLAV MEHTA: Hi, everyone.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.070
Thank you for
attending this session.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:10.410
My name is Pallav Mehta.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.590
And I'm a product manager
on a Cloud AI team.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:16.290
And today I'm going to talk
to you about delivering

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.730
highly personalized
product recommendations

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:21.240
with recommendations
[INAUDIBLE]..

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:22.950
Later in this
session, we'll also

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.980
get to hear from our partners
at BigCommerce and Qubit

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.140
about the success they've
had with rolling out

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.850
recommendations to
their customers.

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:33.890
To begin with, though,
let's acknowledge

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:36.350
the metaphorical
elephant in the room.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:40.410
Customer shopping behavior
has changed for good.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.730
With fewer in-store
shopping visits,

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.540
retailers have had to shore
up their digital storefronts

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.940
and explore new ways
to meaningfully engage

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.800
with their customers.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.350
Delivering a superior
customer experience

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.080
has become even more
of a differentiator

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:58.898
for the early movers.

00:00:58.898 --> 00:01:00.440
And personalized
recommendations have

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.740
emerged as one of the strongest
potential drivers of revenue

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.500
lift.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.730
But as many retailers
have discovered,

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:10.860
delivering
recommendations at scale

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.700
can actually be quite
complex and time consuming.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.520
On the surface, it means
for a given customer

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.520
in a given context, deciding
which item to recommend.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.950
But understanding a
customer, especially

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.220
if you don't have a
lot of data about them

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:30.120
or their habits frequently
change, can be hard.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.190
Customers also jump
between context

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:35.270
as they mull their
shopping decisions.

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:37.790
And helping them discover
new or poorly cataloged

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.740
items in a low-latency
environment

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:43.460
can be especially challenging.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:46.750
Here at Google, we've
developed smart recommendations

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:50.080
into the magic ingredient that
makes our flagship properties

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.980
such a delightful experience.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:56.030
Google Cloud has packaged
together the best of breed

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:58.520
in deep-learning power
of personalization,

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.355
and made it available
to our customers

00:02:00.355 --> 00:02:01.480
through Recommendations AI.

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:07.190
Recommendations AI uses
Google's latest machine

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:09.440
learning architectures
which dynamically

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.340
adapt to real-time
user behavior, changes,

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:16.300
and variables like a
storefront and pricing.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.270
It's a fully managed
service, so there's

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.250
no need to
pre-process your data,

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.790
maintain pipelines,
optimize models,

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:26.010
of provision infrastructure
to deliver at scale.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:29.260
We do it all for
you, automatically.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:32.100
You simply ingest your
data, retrieve, and display

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.820
recommendation results.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:36.920
You can get up and running fast.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.510
And easy-to-use
graphical interface

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:40.170
can help you
integrate your data,

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.110
configure and serve
recommendations,

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:44.820
and monitor system performance.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.720
And recommendations
can be delivered

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:50.140
at sub-hundred [INAUDIBLE]
latency to customers anywhere

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:53.250
in the world, irrespective of
their language or location.

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:57.760
It's a simple three-step
process to make

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:00.640
the most of Recommendations AI.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:04.570
First, put all your data to
work by codelessly ingesting it

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:08.560
into the Recommendations AI by
using Google tools you already

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:10.300
use.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:13.030
Next, select your business
goals through an intuitive

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:18.000
UI with just a few clicks,
and set your models to train.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.330
And finally, serve
recommendations

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:22.010
anywhere in the
customer journey,

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:26.220
across web, mobile,
or email campaigns.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:29.790
As a bonus, we automatically
retrain your models daily

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:32.580
to draw insights from the
changing catalogs, user

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:35.580
behavior, or shopping
trends, and incorporate them

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:39.358
into the recommendations
being served.

00:03:39.358 --> 00:03:41.650
There are two parts to the
data that Recommendations AI

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:45.180
users to train
personalization models.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.220
First, there's a
catalog of items

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:50.820
to recommend that includes
item descriptions, images,

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:53.650
categories, and price.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:56.730
And second, there's
customer and event data,

00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:01.205
that is a history of what users
have clicked on or bought.

00:04:01.205 --> 00:04:02.830
We've made it seamless
for you to bring

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:06.560
your data to Recommendations
AI through a plethora of tools

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:10.840
you already use like Google
Tag Manager, Google Analytics

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:14.090
360, Google Shopping,
or BigQuery,

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:17.170
and are continuously
working on ways to eliminate

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:20.810
the need for you to write a
single line of code to do this.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:23.410
For example, you can now
schedule your frequent catalog

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:25.360
imports from Google
Shopping to keep

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:30.200
your catalog of items and
Recommendations AI up to date.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:33.190
We also monitor the health of
your data feed in real time,

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:38.420
so that you can be notified when
the data quality deteriorates.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:42.140
Next, with just a few clicks in
the Recommendations AI console,

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:44.170
you can specify the
business objectives

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:47.350
you'd like to cater
your recommendations to.

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:50.080
First, select the
recommendation type that's

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:52.490
most relevant for use case.

00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:54.190
For example, the
Recommended For You

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:56.560
model is our most
personalized model

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:59.710
that many of our customers use
in a placement on their home

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:03.770
page or in email campaigns.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.220
Most customers complement
this with the Others You May

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:09.453
Like model, the replacement
on the product detail page,

00:05:09.453 --> 00:05:10.870
and the Frequently
Bought Together

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:15.580
model through a placement
in the Add to Cart pop-up.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:18.708
Next, specify your objective.

00:05:18.708 --> 00:05:20.500
It could be maximizing
a click-through rate

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:23.750
on the recommendation, a
conversion rate, or revenue

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:25.900
per session.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:29.620
And finally, choose from a
plethora of fine-tuning options

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:32.080
that can enable you to
do things like constrain

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.255
the recommendations to
follow certain business

00:05:34.255 --> 00:05:36.520
or merchandising
rules, or increase

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:39.010
the diversification of
items being recommended,

00:05:39.010 --> 00:05:41.860
or increase likelihood that
higher-priced items will

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:43.650
be recommended.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:46.050
Once you hit the Create
button in the console,

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:49.130
in just a couple of days, your
models will be fully trained,

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:51.380
and you'll be able to preview
the recommendations they

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:54.380
are making before deploying
those recommendations

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:57.760
in production.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:59.720
Once your models
are ready to serve,

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:02.420
you can leverage
Recommendations AI anywhere

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.260
in the customer journey.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:06.530
Let's take a look at
one customer's journey

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:09.150
as an example.

00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:11.420
A customer begins their
journey on a laptop,

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:13.750
browsing the sports
apparel category.

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:17.020
But Recommendations
AI recommend shoes.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:20.180
The customer leaves, but comes
back to the site on their phone

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:22.490
to view more shoes.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:26.760
Recommendations AI steps in
again to recommend sunglasses.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:30.060
Our customer adds sunglasses
and shoes to their cart,

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:33.080
indicating an interest
in both items.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.000
Here, Recommendations
AI recommends

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.850
shorts, which the
customer clicks on

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:41.440
to look at, but ultimately,
abandons their cart.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:44.020
Three days later, you can send
a personalized follow-up email

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:47.170
to the customer with recommended
items based on the customer's

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:49.430
clicks and interests.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.550
Recommendations AI
closes the loop,

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:54.840
spurring the customer to buy
sunglasses and shorts, both

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:57.620
recommended, based on the
customer's previous activity

00:06:57.620 --> 00:06:59.780
across devices.

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:02.180
As you can see,
high-quality recommendations

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:05.180
can work throughout the
entire buying process,

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:07.640
from initial product
discovery on a laptop,

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:09.570
to consideration
on a mobile device,

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:12.290
to purchasing, followed
through via email.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:15.140
With Recommendations
AI, delivering anywhere

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:17.510
in the customer journey
also means delivering

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:19.460
to any geographic region.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:24.980
We're globally available, and
the API scales to your needs.

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:26.800
One of the things I'd
like to underscore

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:29.380
is how effective Recommendations
AI's deep learning

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:33.870
models can be at
uncovering shopper intent.

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:36.600
Legacy recommendation
solutions that leverage

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.660
popularity-based or
product-based algorithms

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:42.810
will usually anchor on
items or categories,

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:44.850
but miss the
opportunity to cater

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:48.960
to the individual shopper's
journey altogether.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:52.510
Recommendations AI, on the other
hand, is truly personalized,

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:54.990
and looks back at the
user's shopper journey

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:57.660
to make recommendations to them.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.970
That means if a user has
shown an interest in watches

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:02.070
in the past, even
when they are looking

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:04.890
at a seemingly unrelated
product like a dress,

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:08.010
Recommendations AI knows that
they have a high propensity

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:12.480
to purchase the watch, and
will recommend it to them.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:16.085
And we're always iterating
and always improving.

00:08:16.085 --> 00:08:17.710
They've made it
trivially simple to get

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:21.430
started with Recommendations
AI through the console.

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.470
Any Google Cloud
customer can now

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:25.960
enable the
Recommendations AI API,

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:28.200
and train and manage their
recommendation models

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:30.252
with just a few clicks.

00:08:30.252 --> 00:08:34.370
We're constantly adding easier
ways to ingest your data,

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:38.179
such as with the recent
GA 360 integration.

00:08:38.179 --> 00:08:40.250
We also now
automatically monitor

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:42.860
the quality of your data,
and give you the ability

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:47.300
to preview
recommendations in the UI.

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:50.780
Our models can now create
faster than ever before,

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:53.170
and are retrained daily to
make the most of the changing

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:55.160
patterns in your data.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:09:00.370
We can handle massive catalogs
with tens of millions of items.

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:02.620
In collaboration with some
of our colleagues at Google

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:04.540
Research, we're
pushing the boundary

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.160
of what's possible
for recommendation

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:08.080
systems for retail.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.930
As an example, some of the
work that's come out of that

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.610
has made it possible
for us to correct

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:16.900
for bias with popular items,
seasonality, and leverage item

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:19.510
metadata to make sense
of long-tail items

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:22.300
for which we don't have much
customer click or purchase

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:24.670
data.

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:26.700
But ultimately, all
of this technology

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:30.650
only matters to the extent
that it delivers results.

00:09:30.650 --> 00:09:33.670
As we've been building and
scaling Recommendations AI,

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.420
we've worked with a
number of customers

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:37.430
to roll out better
recommendations

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:41.270
to 100% of their production
e-commerce traffic.

00:09:41.270 --> 00:09:44.330
Along the way, we've been
able to prove our ability

00:09:44.330 --> 00:09:47.330
to deliver a significant
lift on key business metrics

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:50.420
that you care about, as
shown in AV tests controlled

00:09:50.420 --> 00:09:53.180
by our customers, versus
their previous recommendation

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:55.250
systems.

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:57.110
To talk about some
of these results,

00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:59.810
I'd like to introduce
Brian and Graham.

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:03.380
Brian is the CTO of BigCommerce,
one of the largest SAS

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:05.400
e-commerce platforms
in the world,

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:08.390
and an important
Google Cloud partner.

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:11.120
And Graham is the CEO
of Qubit, a leader

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:14.200
in AI-led merchandising and
personalized experiences,

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:19.320
and an early adopter
of Recommendations AI.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:20.550
BRIAN DHATT: Hello, everyone.

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.500
I'm Brian Dhatt, Chief
Technology Officer

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:24.000
at BigCommerce.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:26.820
Today, I'm going to provide a
short overview of BigCommerce,

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:29.670
what we do, and why we're
really excited about Google

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:30.600
Recommendations AI.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.060
I'll then share a
recent case study

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:36.480
on using Google Recommendations
AI with one of our merchants

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:39.010
and some of our
learnings from that.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:41.490
Lastly, we'll talk about what
comes next for BigCommerce

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:43.170
with Google Recommendations AI.

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:48.308
First, to understand
who've M Commerce is,

00:10:48.308 --> 00:10:49.850
it's important to
look at the history

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:51.560
of e-commerce platforms.

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:53.600
Typically, there
were two options

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:57.470
when it came to e-commerce,
open source and SAS.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:00.200
Merchants that favored full
control over the architecture

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:03.110
and build of their
site chose open source.

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:05.260
Merchants that favored
simplicity and security

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:06.980
chose SAS.

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:08.510
That compromise is
really no longer

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:11.810
necessary with BigCommerce's
open SAS approach, which

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:15.500
gives brands the traditional
benefits of multi-tenant SAS,

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:18.790
usability, performance,
continuous upgrades,

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:21.740
with the flexibility
to build and innovate.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.810
Over 90% of our
platform is exposed,

00:11:23.810 --> 00:11:26.090
via APIs, which gives
brands the ability

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:28.600
to extend the platform to
existing tools and solutions

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:30.890
that they might use,
or build completely

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:33.800
custom solutions to
complex problems.

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:35.570
Not only do we provide
these capabilities,

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:37.880
but we take it a step
further by investing heavily

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:40.040
in integrations with
best of breed solutions

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:43.670
and emerging technologies,
like AI, for example.

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:46.190
It's because of our API-driven
architecture and best

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:49.280
of breed approach that we're
here today talking about Google

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:51.260
Recommendations AI.

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:53.870
Let's take a closer look
why this integration

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:56.890
is so exciting for us.

00:11:56.890 --> 00:11:59.350
When we combine Google's
incredible AI technology

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:02.410
with BigCommerce's powerful
e-commerce platform,

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:04.780
incredible things
become possible.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:08.230
We use AI technology to enable
merchants to easily automate

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:10.780
parts of their
merchandising strategy.

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:13.570
Shoppers benefit from being
able to more easily discover

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:15.280
products that they
love, even when

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:17.770
they're browsing through
very large product catalogs.

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:22.870
To prove the efficacy of
Google's AI functionality,

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:26.620
we started partnering with the
brand Woolrich and their agency

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:28.420
MoJo Active.

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:30.220
We created an A/B
test where half

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:33.810
of the shoppers on woolrich.com
got the incumbent experience,

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:35.890
where the Related
Products section was

00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:38.510
powered by a search algorithm.

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:41.440
The other half of shoppers
got the same visual design,

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:44.380
but we used Google's
Recommendations AI

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:47.373
to determine which related
products would show up.

00:12:47.373 --> 00:12:49.540
Our objective was to increase
the click through rate

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:54.440
on related products and,
ultimately, revenue.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:56.180
The results are fantastic.

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:58.040
With Google
Recommendations AI, we

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:01.700
increased the click through rate
by 28% on the Related Products

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:06.380
module, but delivered
an amazing 269%

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:09.350
increase in revenue among
the cohort of shoppers

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:12.410
engagement with the related
product recommendations.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:14.480
Said differently,
this is the revenue

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:18.312
from shoppers purchasing related
products that they clicked on.

00:13:18.312 --> 00:13:20.270
We believe this is just
the beginning of what's

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:23.150
possible to help shoppers
discover products they'll love,

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:25.940
and to help merchants
efficiently and profitably grow

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:28.740
their business.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:31.230
The integration we built
starts by ingesting data

00:13:31.230 --> 00:13:33.750
into Google's AI platform.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:36.690
This included the merchant's
product catalog, as well as

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:39.180
three months of historical
product page view events

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:41.910
for an initial model training.

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:44.960
We continually updated Google
with product catalog data

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:48.030
and product page view data to
keep the machine learning model

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:50.700
up to date, and selected
the Others You May

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:54.100
Like model for the
product detail placement.

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:55.990
Once this model was
built and trained,

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:58.570
we wrapped the Google
predictions API

00:13:58.570 --> 00:14:01.720
into a BigCommerce API.

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:04.390
All aspects of the
integration to Google's AI

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:07.955
are managed by us
within our GCP account.

00:14:07.955 --> 00:14:10.205
Because Woolrich is running
their store in BigCommerce

00:14:10.205 --> 00:14:12.650
and we handle the
data integration,

00:14:12.650 --> 00:14:14.450
Woolrich's agency,
MoJo Active, was

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:17.180
able to get Woolrich
live easily and quickly

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:22.930
with powerful technology, using
a very simple BigCommerce API.

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:24.860
While the results
were fantastic,

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:26.820
we discovered a few
challenges along the way.

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:28.570
Let's take a look at
some of the learnings

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:31.712
and where we're headed next.

00:14:31.712 --> 00:14:33.170
One challenge that
surprised us was

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:37.100
how pervasive and
sophisticated bots had become.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:39.140
We found that over
40% of site traffic

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:40.730
was generated from bots.

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:42.470
And this was a
mixture of good bots

00:14:42.470 --> 00:14:44.960
that identify themselves
and their user agent data,

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:48.720
as well as bad bots that
pretended to be human visitors.

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:50.720
Filtering out the bots
became critical to ensure

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:54.350
that we train the ML model
on human generated data,

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:57.680
and to ensure we had accurate
reporting on the A/B test.

00:14:57.680 --> 00:15:00.440
We used two methods to
improve our bot filtering.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:03.980
One was to improve our use
of user [INAUDIBLE] data,

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:06.150
and the other was to
require JavaScript execution

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:08.270
to trigger events,
as older bots don't

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:10.820
tend to support JavaScript.

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:12.860
In regards to the A/B
testing that we set up,

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:15.350
we found this to be an
incredibly valuable way

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:18.690
to learn fast on what is
and what isn't working,

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:21.365
and ultimately, to prove the
efficacy of the solution,

00:15:21.365 --> 00:15:23.365
and the great results we
achieved with Woolrich.

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:29.110
We are extremely excited about
the results we've seen together

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:30.473
with Woolrich.

00:15:30.473 --> 00:15:32.515
We're now looking to bring
Google Recommendations

00:15:32.515 --> 00:15:35.940
AI to more merchants on
the BigCommerce platform.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:38.440
And we're expanding the depth
and breadth of our integration

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:41.313
with Google Recommendations AI.

00:15:41.313 --> 00:15:43.480
If you're interested in
learning more about creating

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:46.660
personalized shopping
experiences on BigCommerce,

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:50.850
please visit us today at
bigcommerce.com/googlenext.

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:52.600
Thanks for spending a
few minutes with me.

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:54.738
And now with that, I'll
turn it over to Graham.

00:15:54.738 --> 00:15:56.030
GRAHAM COOKE: Thank you, Brian.

00:15:56.030 --> 00:15:56.860
Thank you, Pallav.

00:15:56.860 --> 00:15:58.992
Hi, thanks for all your time.

00:15:58.992 --> 00:15:59.950
My name's Graham Cooke.

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:03.470
I'm CEO and founder of Qubit.

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:05.600
Excited to be presenting
to all of you today.

00:16:05.600 --> 00:16:11.290
I guess this is the new normal
to be presenting from my home

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:14.253
at these wonderful
conferences like Google Next.

00:16:14.253 --> 00:16:15.670
But I'm really
excited to take you

00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:18.850
through how the Qubit
clients are using the Google

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:23.200
Recommendations AI platform, one
of most exciting technologies

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:26.420
we've been working
with in a long time.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.180
So I think it goes
without saying,

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:31.190
we're reaching the tipping point
for digital first commerce.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:35.050
This really means that what I'm
seeing, across our client base,

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:39.190
is that there's just more
and more confirmation

00:16:39.190 --> 00:16:41.830
that we've got to be operating
with the digital first

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:42.670
strategy.

00:16:42.670 --> 00:16:45.830
If you're multi-channel
retailer, you've, in the past,

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:47.497
been thinking about
your biggest stores.

00:16:47.497 --> 00:16:48.913
And you've been
thinking about how

00:16:48.913 --> 00:16:50.830
to look at everything
at a store-first model,

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:52.395
a product-first model.

00:16:52.395 --> 00:16:53.770
But really what
we're seeing now,

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:55.210
it's a digital first model.

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:57.520
More and more businesses
are talking about that.

00:16:57.520 --> 00:16:59.200
How do we work from digital?

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:00.910
And stores are
just, essentially,

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:04.960
an arm of digital
first commerce.

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:08.380
What's driving this is the fact
that it's just gotten massively

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:09.819
accelerated.

00:17:09.819 --> 00:17:12.369
It's been a really
hard six months.

00:17:12.369 --> 00:17:15.250
I know all of us
have really found

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:18.609
it challenging to be
trading in these times.

00:17:18.609 --> 00:17:20.920
But ultimately, what
we've seen, though,

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:25.480
is a 10-year leap
in 90 days' time.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:29.890
And that's a 10-year leap in
the penetration of e-commerce.

00:17:29.890 --> 00:17:33.730
And we're now up in
that 30 to 35-plus

00:17:33.730 --> 00:17:36.100
of total online
spending in e-commerce.

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:38.555
And it's incredibly exciting.

00:17:38.555 --> 00:17:40.180
I mean, what we're
seeing is pure plays

00:17:40.180 --> 00:17:42.070
are doing better than
they've ever done.

00:17:42.070 --> 00:17:45.160
Multi-channel
retailers have never

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.860
seen more sales on e-commerce.

00:17:47.860 --> 00:17:50.470
And, really, what all of
our clients are saying to us

00:17:50.470 --> 00:17:54.050
is, how do we keep
up this performance?

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:58.130
How do we keep the digital
channel performing so well?

00:17:58.130 --> 00:18:02.060
And so what I always talk to
the market, and our customers,

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:04.990
and the industry about
is that, really, part

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:07.750
of this tipping point,
digital commerce experiences

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:10.570
are surpassing the
in-store experience.

00:18:10.570 --> 00:18:13.330
And really, that's because the
digital commerce experience

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:14.860
is powered by AI.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:17.530
The site truly
knows who you are.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:18.850
It's able to understand you.

00:18:18.850 --> 00:18:20.860
It's able to guide you
through the journey.

00:18:20.860 --> 00:18:23.530
It's helping you find the
things and discover the things

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:25.240
you might not have ever found.

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:29.080
And simply walking into a
store, you don't get that.

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:32.055
You don't have that
assistance, when

00:18:32.055 --> 00:18:33.430
you're walking
through the store,

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:35.320
in the same way,
because that store has

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:36.730
been built for
everybody who came

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:38.560
into the physical location.

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:41.320
And the people in that
store don't know you

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:43.220
deeply in many cases.

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:46.000
And so you just don't get
as great an experience.

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:48.340
I find myself walking to
stores now and thinking,

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:50.530
this takes so long
to find what I need,

00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:53.950
compared to how well it
works to shop on many

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:56.120
of our customers' sites.

00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:58.240
So Qubit focuses
on driving growth

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:00.880
by focusing on
relevance for leading

00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:04.990
retail businesses within
fashion, luxury, health

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:06.910
and beauty, grocery.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:08.710
And really what our
customers are doing,

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:12.430
is they're using personalization
and AI-led merchandising

00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:16.190
technology to focus on driving
relevance for their customer.

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:18.850
And by providing more
relevant customer experiences,

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:21.700
those customers spend
more, and come back,

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.110
and become more loyal.

00:19:23.110 --> 00:19:25.210
And our customers
are able to continue

00:19:25.210 --> 00:19:30.670
to be leaders, and continue
to advance as the trendsetting

00:19:30.670 --> 00:19:32.920
brands in the industry.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:35.770
So I'm going to talk about
one of the experiences

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:40.150
that our customer is
using around the AI-led

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:43.510
recommendations, in one
of the most notoriously

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:46.180
difficult parts to
do a recommendation

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:48.230
model, the basket page.

00:19:48.230 --> 00:19:53.770
Now typically, with
your non-one-to-one,

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:58.720
your crowd-based models
for recommendations,

00:19:58.720 --> 00:20:01.390
you show a recommendation
in the basket.

00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:03.130
You're probably going
to drive conversion

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:07.150
down significantly because
you're ultimately distracting

00:20:07.150 --> 00:20:10.480
your customer as they're ready
to check out with something

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:13.390
less relevant, potentially.

00:20:13.390 --> 00:20:15.830
Nobody's been doing
one-to-one in the basket.

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:18.100
And so in many cases,
conversion has gone down.

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:20.260
Maybe basket values have
gone up to make up for it,

00:20:20.260 --> 00:20:21.520
but it hasn't been that good.

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:25.280
What we've seen with using
Google Recommendations

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:28.930
AI in the basket, is
we've seen a 5% increase

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:31.600
in revenue per visitor.

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:34.660
Almost the same conversion
rate, but a big increase in

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:35.628
add to baskets.

00:20:35.628 --> 00:20:37.420
And really, what this
is the equivalent of,

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:39.940
for the first time, and
you're applying it to luxury,

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:42.160
you're applying it to
fashion, you're applying it

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:44.080
to health and beauty,
is you're creating

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:48.700
that impulsive, at the
checkout purchase opportunity,

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:51.868
just like when you're in
an actual physical store,

00:20:51.868 --> 00:20:54.160
and they've put all the items
near the checkout for you

00:20:54.160 --> 00:20:56.410
to just pick them up
and put them on the till

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:57.310
as you're leaving.

00:20:57.310 --> 00:20:59.890
So this is the
equivalent of impulsive,

00:20:59.890 --> 00:21:02.560
completely personalized,
and not distracting.

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:04.050
And it's driving 5%.

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:08.315
Just one recommendation
model carousel doing 5%.

00:21:08.315 --> 00:21:09.940
And typically what
our clients will do,

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:13.240
is they will actually
implement between 5

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:18.100
and 15 various different
AI-powered personalization

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:20.560
recommendations carousels
across their site,

00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:22.120
their app, their emails.

00:21:22.120 --> 00:21:24.880
And the cumulative impact
of this is getting it to be

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:30.070
20%-25% of additional sales from
bringing all these different

00:21:30.070 --> 00:21:32.420
strategies together.

00:21:32.420 --> 00:21:34.720
And really, what our
clients across the base,

00:21:34.720 --> 00:21:37.647
as they're using more
true one-to-one, is

00:21:37.647 --> 00:21:38.980
they're playing that back to us.

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:42.310
They're saying, for the
first time have we actually

00:21:42.310 --> 00:21:45.250
seen what one-to-one
recommendations,

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:47.800
one-to-one personalization
does for revenue.

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:49.420
It drives more revenue
than we've ever

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:50.950
been able to drive before.

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:53.020
And really, what I'm
seeing is this leap

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:55.690
from where we've
been all these years.

00:21:55.690 --> 00:21:58.613
We've just been stuck
underneath this impact barrier.

00:21:58.613 --> 00:22:00.280
And now we're able
to break through this

00:22:00.280 --> 00:22:04.180
with the real AI, real
individualization at scale.

00:22:04.180 --> 00:22:07.240
And it's thanks to platforms
like Google Recommendations AI

00:22:07.240 --> 00:22:09.088
that we're really
able to do this.

00:22:09.088 --> 00:22:10.880
And what we want to
give for our customers,

00:22:10.880 --> 00:22:12.380
we want to give
them the combination

00:22:12.380 --> 00:22:14.730
of the power of the
Google Recommendations AI.

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:19.000
But we want to give them within
the merchandising Control

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:24.460
Suite, so that they can
control how the recommendation

00:22:24.460 --> 00:22:27.010
system will actually
work, how they can exclude

00:22:27.010 --> 00:22:30.280
certain products, include other
products, the type of model

00:22:30.280 --> 00:22:33.490
they want to use, and exactly
how it's going to look,

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:36.440
based on the different page
templates and strategies.

00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:39.220
And this is the relationship
between merchandisers

00:22:39.220 --> 00:22:44.350
and the AI that we think allows
merchandising teams to really

00:22:44.350 --> 00:22:47.170
just accelerate, and
become more proactive,

00:22:47.170 --> 00:22:50.380
and become the great
merchandisers they are, and not

00:22:50.380 --> 00:22:53.450
have to be constantly
working behind the customer.

00:22:53.450 --> 00:22:55.180
They're working
ahead of the customer

00:22:55.180 --> 00:22:56.700
with this type of technology.

00:22:56.700 --> 00:22:58.450
And then we marry that
up with other types

00:22:58.450 --> 00:23:02.710
of personalized content, other
type of badging, scarcity,

00:23:02.710 --> 00:23:06.220
all within a single
easy-to-use platform.

00:23:06.220 --> 00:23:08.230
And so under the
hood, what's actually

00:23:08.230 --> 00:23:12.310
happening is Qubit is providing
a clean, contextually-relevant

00:23:12.310 --> 00:23:16.492
data feed, in real time, to
the Google Recommendations AI.

00:23:16.492 --> 00:23:18.700
And so what that really
looks like, here on the left,

00:23:18.700 --> 00:23:20.990
is it's an
industry-specific taxonomy.

00:23:20.990 --> 00:23:23.500
So whether you're in
fashion, or you're

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:26.170
in luxury, or health
and beauty, or grocery,

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:30.190
we have an event-based taxonomy,
specific to your industry.

00:23:30.190 --> 00:23:34.870
And that allows you to feed
this deep, contextual, real time

00:23:34.870 --> 00:23:37.730
flow of information about
customers, about products,

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:42.600
about transactions into the deep
learning AI system by the API.

00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:44.350
And then all the
learning and the training

00:23:44.350 --> 00:23:46.740
happens on an
individual customer,

00:23:46.740 --> 00:23:50.470
at an individual shopper
at the brand level.

00:23:50.470 --> 00:23:53.260
And that's what starts to create
this incredible recommendation

00:23:53.260 --> 00:23:57.460
system that, then, flows
back into that merchandising

00:23:57.460 --> 00:23:59.630
and experience workflow tool.

00:23:59.630 --> 00:24:02.140
So the merchandiser can
control how it's going to look.

00:24:02.140 --> 00:24:03.380
They can control the rules.

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:05.380
And most important, they
can measure the results

00:24:05.380 --> 00:24:08.650
and understand if this
type of personalization

00:24:08.650 --> 00:24:12.550
is effective at driving
sales or conversions,

00:24:12.550 --> 00:24:14.110
and helping to
grow the business.

00:24:14.110 --> 00:24:16.000
And then this is a
constant feedback loop,

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:20.200
from merchandiser feeding
context back into the system,

00:24:20.200 --> 00:24:24.070
and that goes back into the
recommendations learning

00:24:24.070 --> 00:24:25.640
system.

00:24:25.640 --> 00:24:28.600
And so we've been a partner
of Google Cloud for over five

00:24:28.600 --> 00:24:30.770
years, and we've
never looked back.

00:24:30.770 --> 00:24:32.740
It's the most phenomenal
cloud platform.

00:24:32.740 --> 00:24:35.440
It's the most advanced for
handling real time data

00:24:35.440 --> 00:24:36.520
systems like this.

00:24:36.520 --> 00:24:38.010
And it's the only
way we could have

00:24:38.010 --> 00:24:42.565
scaled what we've built for all
of our hundreds of customers.

00:24:42.565 --> 00:24:44.440
And really what we're
handling here, at peak,

00:24:44.440 --> 00:24:46.760
is 120,000 events per second.

00:24:46.760 --> 00:24:48.880
We are processing
enormous amounts

00:24:48.880 --> 00:24:52.840
of information on
the peak sales days

00:24:52.840 --> 00:24:55.360
that we're all coming
up to in holiday.

00:24:55.360 --> 00:24:58.120
It takes us, as
well, just a second

00:24:58.120 --> 00:25:00.310
to take all that real
time information that's

00:25:00.310 --> 00:25:02.500
just flowing through it,
that hundreds of thousands

00:25:02.500 --> 00:25:06.130
per second, and put that
into the systems that

00:25:06.130 --> 00:25:09.220
will be key to how the data
is trained within the Google

00:25:09.220 --> 00:25:13.210
Recommendations AI,
